        <div class="drivers">Economic pressure from sustained oil-export disruption, IRGC overextension in Hormuz gatekeeping role, and elite factional fracture between diplomatic track (Araghchi/Pezeshkian) and hardline track (Fars/IRGC). The MOU negotiation proximity creates a secondary fragility: if a deal is announced and then repudiated by Khamenei's office, domestic political legitimacy of the pragmatist faction collapses; conversely, a signed deal reduces near-term collapse probability by providing an economic relief valve. No change this week (weekly cadence).</div>
      </div>

